ther collections of particles.", "display_url": "go.aps.org/4kery4l", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/4kery4l", "images": [{"height": 250, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113670376131534849/pe4La2Tp?format=png&name=orig", "width": 500}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113670376131534849/pe4La2Tp?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 251, "status": 200, "title": "Tiny Particles Charge Like Capacitors", "unwound_url": "https://physics.aps.org/articles/v19/143", "url": "https://t.co/IXSVSBa0Vb"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/V6NxmbcSoz", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/PhysicsMagazine/status/2113670371115171986/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113670368325931008", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/V6NxmbcSoz"}]}, "id": "2113670371115171986", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 915, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "By measuring repeated collisions between a pair of levitated particles, researchers found that triboelectric charging follows a universal pattern over longer times — insights that could improve models of charging in real-world phenomena. \n\nRead more: https://t.co/IXSVSBa0Vb https://t.co/V6NxmbcSoz", "url": "https://x.com/PhysicsMagazine/status/2113670371115171986"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113669331632451584"]}, "author_id": "14499829", "created_at": "2026-10-23T16:30:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113669334757159030"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MrcusyIDW1", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/WHO/status/2113669334757159030/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113669331632451584", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/MrcusyIDW1"}]}, "id": "2113669334757159030", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 33085, "like_count": 120, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 49}, "text": "When extreme heat strikes, how many people become ill or die? \n \nToo 